body:
This PR attempts to fix #367

We have a bit of a problem. `UTF8` came from these lines

``` java
        try (InputStreamReader reader = openFile(fileToOpen, suppliedEncoding, fallbackEncoding)) {
            BibtexParser bp = new BibtexParser(reader);

            ParserResult pr = bp.parse();
            pr.setEncoding(reader.getEncoding());
```

It is set in [this method call](https://docs.oracle.com/javase/8/docs/api/java/io/InputStreamReader.html#getEncoding--). That's the Java API. The `InputStreamReader` says that the proper name of the encoding is `UTF8`. 

My solution is an ugly compatibility hack in which we just insert the `-` manually. Ugly, but works... What do you think?

Fixed encoding problem in Test when running gradle check
Follow up from #1014 

@tobiasdiez

@kojiyokota I was so kind and fixed the language files for you. You had some duplicates in there, probably resulted in conflicts from merging

@koppor  We could merge this and then @kojiyokota can update the missing strings again as new pr.

